## Why This Is Asked
Examines practical isolation controls for logs in multi-tenant cloud-native systems, including data-minimization, policy enforcement, and incident response.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped logging
- ABAC/OPA policy enforcement at ingestion
- Data redaction and least-privilege exporters
- SPIRE/mTLS between log agents and collectors
- Ephemeral credentials rotation and secrets hygiene

## Code Example
```javascript
function redactForTenant(log, tenantId) {
  const redacted = {...log};
  const sensitiveKeys = ['ssn','creditCard','dob','email'];
  for (const k of sensitiveKeys) {
    if (redacted[k] && redacted.tenantId === tenantId) {
      redacted[k] = '[REDACTED]';
    }
  }
  return redacted;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test for cross-tenant access in search results?
- What monitoring signals indicate redaction failures or policy drift?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical application of phishing-resistant MFA and device-based access in admin contexts, plus rollout, exceptions, and measurable outcomes.

## Key Concepts

- phishing-resistant MFA (FIDO2/WebAuthn)
- passwordless SSO
- device posture (MDM/EMM)
- conditional access rules
- centralized logging (SIEM) and phishing simulations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example simple authorization gate
function allowAccess(user, device) {
  const okUser = user.isAdmin;
  const okDevice = device.isCompliant;
  const okMFA = user.mfaCompletedWithFido2;
  return okUser && okDevice && okMFA;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle a lost FIDO key or key compromise?
- What metrics would you track to gauge phishing-resistant MFA effectiveness?
